1
00:05:17,647 --> 00:05:23,647
What happens in the world's largest trash city will transform you.

2
00:10:35,294 --> 00:10:41,294
Waste Land is a documentary film directed by Lucy Walker.

3
00:15:52,941 --> 00:15:58,941
An uplifting feature documentary highlighting the transformative
power of art and the beauty of the human spirit.

4
00:21:10,588 --> 00:21:16,588
Top-selling contemporary artist Vik Muniz takes us on an emotional journey from Jardim Gramacho, the world's
largest landfill on the outskirts of Rio de Janeiro, to the heights of international art stardom.

5
00:26:28,235 --> 00:26:34,235
Vik collaborates with the brilliant catadores, pickers of recyclable materials, true Shakespearean characters
who live and work in the garbage quoting Machiavelli and showing us how to recycle ourselves.

6
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Himself, played by Vik Muniz.

7
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Waste Land (Portuguese: Lixo Extraordinário, lit.

8
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
'Extraordinary Garbage') is a 2010 British-Brazilian documentary film directed by Lucy Walker,
co-directed by João Jardim and Karen Harley, and produced by Angus Aynsley and Hank Levine.

9
00:47:38,823 --> 00:47:44,823
The music for the film was created by Moby, who is a
friend and frequent collaborator of Walker.

10
00:52:56,470 --> 00:53:02,470
The film follows artist Vik Muniz as he travels to the world's largest landfill in Jardim Gramacho, just outside Rio de Janeiro, to collaborate with a lively group
of "catadores" (workers who salvage recyclable materials from the garbage) to make contemporary art using some of the materials they have "picked".

11
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:20,117
Muniz donated the proceeds from the sale of his pictures of the artworks to the ACAMJG (Associação dos Catadores do Aterro Metropolitano de Jardim Gramacho, or Association of Pickers of the Metropolitan Landfill of Jardim Gramacho),
which is a co-operative founded and led by Sebastião "Tião" Carlos Dos Santos, one of the catadores involved in the art project; the prize money from the awards won by the film was also donated to the organization.

12
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
The film premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on 24 January 2010.

13
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
It was distributed by Arthouse Films in the US, Entertainment One in Canada,
Hopscotch Films in Australia and New Zealand, and Midas Filmes in Portugal.

14
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
The film won over 50 film awards, including the International Documentary Association's Best Documentary Award (which was handed to
director Lucy Walker inside a garbage bag), and was nominated for Best Documentary Feature at the 83rd Academy Awards.

15
01:19:24,705 --> 01:19:30,705
The film explores themes of garbage, empowerment,
rio de janeiro, artist, dead child.

16
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
